{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1111086-caerns","id":1111086,"title":"Caerns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-03T18:12:47-07:00","id":1111086,"title":"Caerns","content":"Ok, I have 2 questions for the group. Any help would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> 1) I have a very hard time as a ST visualizing a caern. It's not that I don't &quot;get it&quot;, it's that I can't extend the game knowledge to actual geography. Can someone help me understand how you see a caern using a real location that I can set as sort of a template?<br /> <br /> 2) Part of the current story involves a rage caern in Russia. How would you visualize such a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T19:13:07-07:00","id":1111108,"title":"","content":"A caern is simply a sacred site. It could be anything and anywhere. A caern essentially is a Garou temple, but it is usually not a physical building that Garou build as humans would build a cathedral, temple, or mosque.<br /> <br /> Caerns have to be big enough to include various areas - bawns, shrines, living areas, grave of hallowed heroes, the assembly area, and the caern's heart itself. So it's the entire geographic area - not just the &quot;building of the temple/church/etc&quot;, but the property it is built on, the parking lot, and any other number of things.<br /> <br /> The Bawn of the caern, which is just a word which means the geographical limits/perimeter of the caern. This delineates where the sacred site begins and ends. This is border is generally static, increasing or decreasing only if the caern's power/rating changes. Think of it more like a political boundary. Since the Bawn marks the area where the Garou will begin to defend the caern against potential threats, this affects things.<br /> <br /> The grave of hallowed heroes are where the greatest heroes of the sept are buried, it's basically the parish cemetery attached to the local church except only a few select Garou are buried there.<br /> <br /> The living area is the place on larger caerns where sept members could potentially live. It could be anything from natural formations (like caves, burrows, dens) to actual physical structures (a tent, a tipi, a treehouse, a farmhouse, a meadhall, a camping trailer, or anything else that the sept finds appropriate. Small caerns typically do not have an living area as there is no room in which case Garou attempt to find lodging as close as possible.<br /> <br /> Shrines are simply a place where the Garou can meditate and pray. It's like the chapel room. Nothing It can be anything - a spot overlooking an area under a nice shade tree, a cleared area with a totem pole, or an actual room/building. There can be multiple shrines at a caern. Sometimes individual packs create their own shrines so that it is particularly appropriate to their pack totem.<br /> <br /> The assembly area is where the entire sept can meet to conduct the moot. This is the social heart of the sept, It is where people meet, discuss business, challenge each other, and councils are kept. It's like the old Roman forum. It could potentially be anything as long it fits the caern's concept, and is large enough to host the entire sept plus any visiting Garou. Think about what would people want when they get together. They may want some kind of obvious focal point where leaders perform the key moot tasks. They may want some kind of obvious sign of where the assembly area begins and ends, like standing stones, actual seating, pathstones, ditches, or something else.<br /> <br /> All of the above are actually mundane areas. There is nothing special about them, other than that they are officially part of the caern.<br /> <br /> The Caern Heart, and only the Caern Heart, is the actual SPIRITUAL CENTER of the caern. This is where the caern totem resides. This is where the spirit world meets the realm, where the gauntlet becomes thin, and where the Ritemaster can access the caern's power. The Caern Heart does not need to be geographically in the center of the caern. It could be anywhere, perhaps near the Bawn. The Caern Heart could look like anything. Maybe it's a sacred grove, or a natural wellspring, or a single tree, or a column of stone, or where wind meets in a valley. A caern might have multiple caern hearts - this is rare, but it does happen. In which case the sept helps/assists multiple caern totems when they perform their moots.<br /> <br /> Usually, most Garou caerns will be far away from humanity deep in the wilderness. That is not always the case, and urban caerns often have to deal with the problem of ordinary humans walking not only onto the bawn, but throughout the entire caern as well. In the canonical Sept of the Green in New York City, all of Central Park is the bawn and the caern hearts are located at the Bethesda Fountain and Turtle Pond.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you are looking for ideas for a Caern of Rage, you need to think of what kind of place would attract a spirit of Rage. It would have to be a place associated with violence, death, battle, anger, and ferocity. It might be a natural place like an active volcano with a boiling caldera, or a site where a particularly awful battle took place, or which has been the place of many battles. Or where a gruesome massacre or atrocity took place. Such kill areas do not necessarily need to be human. Perhaps it is a place where hunters routinely slaughtered Pleistocene megafauna, or something like the La Brea tar pits which gruesomely trapped many kills before suffocating them. Or perhaps where a meteor impact once hit very violently.<br /> <br /> Once you conceive of what kind of area would attract a rage spirit, then you can figure out the caern heart (the actual place of spiritual power) and then determine all the rest later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-18-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T19:59:48-07:00","id":1111124,"title":"","content":"Black Fox, <br /> <br /> Thank you very much for taking the time to square me away. That's a fantastic answer, and it clears up a lot of confusion for me. I just couldn't wrap my head around the layout and you made it made sense. I hope I can return the favor sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}